[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Fault Detection, Isolation, Recovery, and Hardware Slot Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-FDIR-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Uploadable Table-Driven Debounced Watchpoints
STATEMENT: >>>
The FDIR engine (FdirEngine) shall evaluate table-driven Watchpoint definitions (GreaterThan, LessThan, EqualTo, NotEqualTo, OutOfRange) against live telemetry channels with configurable consecutive-sample persistence debounce counts, uploadable via ParamBank without recompiling flight software.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Table-driven watchpoints with debounce eliminate false positives from single-sample sensor glitches and allow in-flight threshold tuning as hardware ages.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/fdir_slot_mgr/include/strata/services/fdir/fdir_engine.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-FDIR-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Boolean Actionpoints and Multi-Level Recovery Escalation Ladder
STATEMENT: >>>
The FDIR engine shall evaluate boolean Actionpoint rules (AllOf or AnyOf watchpoint bitmasks) and emit deterministic RecoveryDirectives escalating across five levels: LocalWarn, WarmRestartPartition, QuiesceAndReloadSlot, FailoverSpareSlot, and SystemSafeMode.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A bounded escalation ladder contains local anomalies at the lowest disruptive tier while guaranteeing deterministic progression when repeated recoveries fail.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/fdir_slot_mgr/include/strata/services/fdir/fdir_engine.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-FDIR-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Dual-Layer Partition Heartbeat and Hardware Slot Watchdog Monitor
STATEMENT: >>>
The FDIR subsystem shall provide a HealthMonitor that monitors monotonic per-partition Blackboard heartbeats and hypervisor CPU overrun flags in software while verifying that every active PL slot kicks its hardware SCSR.WDT_RELOAD timer within its configured timeout window.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Combining passive Blackboard liveness monitoring with autonomous hardware slot watchdogs prevents intrusive ping traffic while guaranteeing safe hardware quiesce if a guest hangs.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/fdir_slot_mgr/include/strata/services/fdir/health_and_fault_router.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-FDIR-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Isolated FaultRouter for Partition Traps and Assertions
STATEMENT: >>>
The FDIR subsystem shall provide a FaultRouter receiving hypervisor exception dumps and guest FaultReport notifications, logging compact crash records, and executing isolated partition restart for Class C/D faults while reserving spacecraft safe-mode escalation exclusively for unrecoverable Class B TCB faults.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An assertion or fault inside a science payload must never propagate into a spacecraft-wide reboot.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/fdir_slot_mgr/include/strata/services/fdir/health_and_fault_router.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-FDIR-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: CRAM Upset Frame-to-Slot Attribution and Surgical Recovery
STATEMENT: >>>
The FDIR engine shall map physical configuration-memory upset frame addresses from Versal PMC XilSEM or an external Kintex rad-hard scrubber to their owning PL slot ID, issuing surgical QuiesceAndReloadSlot directives for dynamic slots and SystemSafeMode only for uncorrectable upsets outside mapped dynamic regions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Exact frame-to-slot attribution prevents an uncorrectable upset in one instrument partition from disturbing Class B avionics or sibling spatial instruments.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/fdir_slot_mgr/include/strata/services/fdir/fdir_engine.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-FDIR-006
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Pre-Verified Offline Reconfiguration Matrix and Spare-Slot Failover
STATEMENT: >>>
When a primary hardware slot exceeds its configured reload threshold, the FDIR engine shall consult a pre-verified SlotFailoverEntry table and emit a FailoverSpareSlot directive migrating the instrument personality and its CriticalStore checkpoint to a designated spare DFX slot and standby partition.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Deterministic offline failover tables provide rapid, verifiable hardware redundancy against permanent hard faults without complex online placement heuristics.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/fdir_slot_mgr/include/strata/services/fdir/fdir_engine.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-FDIR-007
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Authenticated End-to-End DFX and AIE SlotManager
STATEMENT: >>>
The SlotManager shall orchestrate the complete hardware slot lifecycle (Unloaded -> Loading -> Sbit -> Standby -> Active -> Quiescing -> Faulted), enforcing cryptographic digest verification (SHA-384 / RSA-4096 or ECDSA-P384), bounded quiesce timeouts, hardware NoC INI or DFX Decoupler isolation, Versal PMC PLM or Kintex DMA ICAPE3 loading, and SCSR MANIFEST_HASH validation.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Centralizing authenticated partial reconfiguration in a single Class B SlotManager prevents unauthorized or corrupted bitstreams from compromising the shared FPGA fabric.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Demonstration
ARTIFACT: services/fdir_slot_mgr/include/strata/services/fdir/slot_manager.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Zero-Copy Data Products, 64-Bit File Storage, and CCSDS CFDP

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-STOR-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Zero-Copy 64-Byte Data Product Header and Container
STATEMENT: >>>
The storage service shall define a 64-byte cache-line-aligned DpHeader carrying magic, monotonic product ID, container ID, priority, compression algorithm tag, start/end TAI timestamps, 64-bit payload byte length, and CRC-32C checksums stamped directly onto FrameLease payloads without CPU copying.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Zero-copy container framing enables multi-Gbps science recording directly from DDR4/HBM pools into non-volatile solid-state storage.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/storage/include/strata/services/storage/data_products.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-STOR-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Priority-Driven 64-Bit Data Product Catalog with Eviction and Resume
STATEMENT: >>>
The storage service shall provide a crash-safe 64-bit DpCatalog selecting the highest-priority oldest pending product for downlink, tracking 64-bit partial downlink resume offsets across interrupted ground passes, and automatically evicting strictly lower-priority oldest products when storage reaches capacity.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Priority-aware eviction protects high-value science products during long communication blackouts while 64-bit offsets support multi-gigabyte radar and hyperspectral datasets.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/storage/include/strata/services/storage/data_products.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-STOR-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Optional Hardware PL Compression Pipeline Stage
STATEMENT: >>>
The Data Product writer shall support routing a 32-byte FrameDesc through a hardware programmable logic compression slot (such as CCSDS-123.0-B-2, LZ4, or Zstd) before non-volatile storage DMA commit without touching payload bytes on the CPU.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Offloading high-rate science compression to FPGA fabric maximizes solid-state recorder capacity and downlink yield without saturating flight CPU cores.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Demonstration
ARTIFACT: services/storage/include/strata/services/storage/pl_compression_stage.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-STOR-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: 64-Bit Partition-Jailed File Service and DFX Staging Authentication
STATEMENT: >>>
The FileService shall enforce per-partition logical volume ownership and 64-bit byte quotas, support onboard file management operations (commit, move, delete, directory listing, CRC-32C verification), and require explicit authentication on staged DFX/PDI images before SlotManager marks them loadable.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Per-partition storage jails prevent a runaway science partition from filling flight recorder flash or tampering with critical boot and bitstream staging volumes.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/storage/include/strata/services/storage/file_and_cfdp.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-STOR-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: 64-Bit CCSDS CFDP Class 1 and Class 2 Transfer Engine
STATEMENT: >>>
The storage service shall implement CCSDS 727.0-B-5 CFDP Class 1 (unacknowledged) and Class 2 (acknowledged) uplink and downlink transactions with 64-bit file offsets, out-of-order byte-extent coalescing, missing-gap NAK generation, selective retransmission, and suspend/resume checkpointing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Standards-compliant 64-bit CFDP enables reliable transfer of multi-gigabyte science products and partial FPGA bitstreams over intermittent deep-space links.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/storage/include/strata/services/storage/file_and_cfdp.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-STOR-006
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Lightweight Fast File Chunk Uplink and Downlink Protocol
STATEMENT: >>>
In addition to full CCSDS CFDP, the storage service shall provide a minimal chunked file uplink/downlink service with inter-file link cooldown throttling for rapid benchtop FlatSat testing and high-SNR links.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A lightweight fast file protocol simplifies integration testing while cooldown delays prevent continuous file transfers from saturating command links.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/storage/include/strata/services/storage/file_and_cfdp.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-STOR-007
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Refresh-Free Radiation-Hardened Reboot-Surviving Flight Log (TMR + SECDED)
STATEMENT: >>>
The middleware and storage subsystem shall provide a reboot-surviving circular flight log (NvFaultLog) designed for refresh-free non-volatile or radiation-hardened memory blocks (MRAM, FRAM, NVSRAM, or battery-backed SRAM placed in a dedicated .nv_flight_log NOLOAD linker section), featuring a 2-of-3 majority-voted TMR control header, per-word Hamming(72,64) SECDED ECC with in-place single-bit healing and double-bit detection, record CRC-32C, torn-write commit fences, monotonic boot-epoch continuity across cold power cycles, and O(1) incremental background scrubbing.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
DRAM loses contents without refresh during power cycles, watchdogs, and brownouts; a refresh-free TMR+SECDED non-volatile memory block guarantees post-mortem crash dumps, trap registers, and reboot markers survive both radiation upsets and full power loss.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: middleware/include/strata/ipc/nv_fault_log.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Isolated Onboard Autonomy Sandbox

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-AUTO-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Hardware-Isolated Autonomy Sandbox with Step Budget and Opcode Allowlist
STATEMENT: >>>
The AutonomySandbox shall execute uploaded onboard autonomy logic exclusively inside an isolated lower-criticality partition enforcing a hard per-tick execution step budget, Read-Only telemetry snapshot access, and a strict command opcode allowlist that blocks unauthorized critical commands.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Isolating uploaded autonomy scripts from the Class B C&DH address space enables agile onboard science triggering without expanding the flight-critical assurance boundary.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/autonomy_sandbox/include/strata/services/autonomy/sandbox_runner.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-AUTO-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Cryptographically Signed Ahead-of-Time Autonomy Module Loader
STATEMENT: >>>
The autonomy subsystem shall support loading cryptographically verified ahead-of-time compiled WebAssembly or bounded bytecode modules from a jailed storage volume into the isolated AutonomySandbox partition without requiring a dynamic JIT compiler or heap allocator.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Signed AOT modules deliver near-native onboard autonomy performance while preserving zero-heap determinism and uplink security.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Demonstration
ARTIFACT: services/autonomy_sandbox/include/strata/services/autonomy/aot_loader.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-001

[[/SECTION]]
